id: query-options
title: Query Options
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One of the best ways to share "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" between multiple places, yet keep them co-located to one another, is to use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" helper. At runtime, this helper just returns whatever you pass into it, but it has a lot of advantages when using it "},{"type":"link","href":"../typescript.md#typing-query-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"with TypeScript"}]},{"type":"text","value":". You can define all possible options for a query in one place, and you'll also get type inference and type safety for all of them."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { queryOptions } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction groupOptions(id: number) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['groups', id],\n    queryFn: () => fetchGroups(id),\n    staleTime: 5 * 1000,\n  })\n}\n\n// usage:\n\nuseQuery(() => groupOptions(1))\nuseQueries(() => ({\n  queries: [groupOptions(1), groupOptions(2)],\n}))\nqueryClient.query(groupOptions(23))\nqueryClient.setQueryData(groupOptions(42).queryKey, newGroups)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For Infinite Queries, a separate "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/functions/infiniteQueryOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"infiniteQueryOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" helper is available."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can still override some options at the component level. A very common and useful pattern is to create per-component "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" functions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Type inference still works, so query.data will be the return type of select instead of queryFn\n\nconst groupQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n  ...groupOptions(1),\n  select: (data) => data.groupName,\n}))","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nOne of the best ways to share `queryKey` and `queryFn` between multiple places, yet keep them co-located to one another, is to use the `queryOptions` helper. At runtime, this helper just returns whatever you pass into it, but it has a lot of advantages when using it [with TypeScript](../typescript.md#typing-query-options). You can define all possible options for a query in one place, and you'll also get type inference and type safety for all of them.\n\n\n\n```ts\nimport { queryOptions } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction groupOptions(id: number) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['groups', id],\n    queryFn: () => fetchGroups(id),\n    staleTime: 5 * 1000,\n  })\n}\n\n// usage:\n\nuseQuery(() => groupOptions(1))\nuseQueries(() => ({\n  queries: [groupOptions(1), groupOptions(2)],\n}))\nqueryClient.query(groupOptions(23))\nqueryClient.setQueryData(groupOptions(42).queryKey, newGroups)\n```\n\n\n\nFor Infinite Queries, a separate [`infiniteQueryOptions`](../reference/functions/infiniteQueryOptions.md) helper is available.\n\n\n\nYou can still override some options at the component level. A very common and useful pattern is to create per-component `select` functions:\n\n\n\n\n```ts\n// Type inference still works, so query.data will be the return type of select instead of queryFn\n\nconst groupQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n  ...groupOptions(1),\n  select: (data) => data.groupName,\n}))\n```\n\n\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: query-options\ntitle: Query Options\nref: docs/framework/react/guides/query-options.md\nreplace:\n  {\n    '@tanstack/react-query': '@tanstack/solid-query',\n    'useMutationState[(]': 'useMutationState(() => ',\n    'useMutation[(]': 'useMutation(() => ',\n    'useQuery[(]': 'useQuery(() => ',\n    'useQueries[(]': 'useQueries(() => ',\n    'useInfiniteQuery[(]': 'useInfiniteQuery(() => ',\n  }\n---\n\n[//]: # 'Example1'\n\n```ts\nimport { queryOptions } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction groupOptions(id: number) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['groups', id],\n    queryFn: () => fetchGroups(id),\n    staleTime: 5 * 1000,\n  })\n}\n\n// usage:\n\nuseQuery(() => groupOptions(1))\nuseQueries(() => ({\n  queries: [groupOptions(1), groupOptions(2)],\n}))\nqueryClient.query(groupOptions(23))\nqueryClient.setQueryData(groupOptions(42).queryKey, newGroups)\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example1'\n[//]: # 'SelectDescription'\n\nYou can still override some options at the component level. A very common and useful pattern is to create per-component `select` functions:\n\n[//]: # 'SelectDescription'\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n\n```ts\n// Type inference still works, so query.data will be the return type of select instead of queryFn\n\nconst groupQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n  ...groupOptions(1),\n  select: (data) => data.groupName,\n}))\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n"}
